4. Traditional Programming vs Machine Learning

Traditional Programming: Relies on fixed rules (e.g., “if message contains ‘lottery’ → mark as spam”). Effective but rigid, requiring constant manual updates.

Machine Learning: Learns from datasets of spam vs non-spam messages. Extracts patterns (word frequency, sender behavior, message length) and adapts to new spam types automatically.

Key Difference: Traditional programming = rules-based. Machine learning = data-driven learning.
